{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"B\n    \n      querySelectorAll Scanner\n      Select all text-containing elements via CSS selectors (p, span, div, h1-h6, li, td, input, textarea). Check each element's textContent, detect direction, apply fixes.\n      \n        Pros\n          Simple and familiar API\n          Easy to define element scope\n        \n        Cons\n          Selects elements without text too\n          Can miss dynamically added elements\n          Harder to avoid double-processing","choice":"b","id":null,"timestamp":1774886036012}
{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"A\n    \n      TreeWalker Scanner (Recommended)\n      Use document.createTreeWalker() to efficiently walk text nodes. Group by parent element, detect direction per element, apply fixes. MutationObserver watches for new nodes and feeds them back through the same pipeline.\n      \n        Pros\n          Native browser API — very fast\n          Skips non-text nodes automatically\n          Minimal memory allocation\n          Natural fit with MutationObserver\n        \n        Cons\n          Slightly more complex initial setup","choice":"a","id":null,"timestamp":1774886037114}
